  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the **exact solutions** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(2x-{90}^{\u2218})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},$ for ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218},$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{\u2218},\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{\u2218},\\,{x}_{3}=$\n{{field-3}}${}^{\u2218},\\,{x}_{4}=$\n{{field-4}}${}^{\u2218}.$",
  "worked_solution": "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={60}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={30}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {90}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\u2026,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={30}^{\u2218}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={120}^{\u2218}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x={210}^{\u2218}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x={300}^{\u2218}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218}.$ \n\nSo, the solutions to the equation, in ascending order, are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={30}^{\u2218},\\,{x}_{2}={120}^{\u2218},\\,{x}_{3}={210}^{\u2218},\\,{x}_{4}={300}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
